DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't chase Monday's AI bounce.</b> The S&P rose 0.7% on Anthropic's IPO filing, but new lows still beat new highs about 3 to 1. Keep regular investing (DCA) instead of big one-off bets before the Fed and BoT (both Wed) and Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon earnings.",
"<b>Watch oil, not just AI.</b> Brent eased to ~$115.8 on Iran peace talks, but it is still near a six-month high and Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia continue; higher fuel feeds inflation and rate-hike odds.",
"<b>Spread your risk.</b> Big AI firms are raising huge sums (Meta's $95B stock sale, $63B for Anthropic's chips); broad index funds beat betting on single names into earnings.",
"<b>Cash and short-term bonds still pay.</b> The 10Y is near 5%; short-term deposits and bonds are a fine place to wait.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It is back just above $4,000; keep only a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is hovering around $80k; below ~$78k support, expect more downside.",
"<b>Thai investors: be selective.</b> The SET rose 1.05% to 1,579.03 on foreign buying and strong exports, with resistance near 1,590; the BoT is expected to hold at 1.00% Wednesday. In our dividend table, SPALI, TVO, PTT, ICHI and AP trade at or below their buy zones (green), while TOP, TCAP, TASCO and TISCO are well above; check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 27.1 = Fear (after Monday's close), up from 21.0 Extreme Fear and from 20.8 a week ago, as stocks bounced and volatility eased; investors are still cautious about oil, rates and AI spending."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~45 = Elevated, about flat: regional envoys met Iran's leaders in Tehran and the Oleshky truce starts, but Trump named an Iranian nuclear-linked site as a possible target."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 25.4 = fear (up from extreme fear): Monday's 0.7% gain pulled the S&P back toward its trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 23.4 = more lows than highs, extreme fear (58 NYSE highs vs 158 lows Monday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 25.8 = fear: buying improved Monday but is still weak."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 22.8 = many still buying protection, a fearful sign."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 39.6 = fear, better than last week's extreme fear as volatility eased."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 11.0 = bonds have beaten stocks, extreme fear."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 41.6 = fear: lenders are still cautious."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 64 (flat): Trump says it's 'decision time' on Iran and named a buried nuclear-linked site as a possible target, but has said no strikes before the 3 Nov midterms. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 38 (down from 39), the biggest weight: the Oleshky local truce starts 27 Oct and talks are set for November, though both sides trade strike accusations."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 66 (flat): Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia continue, the coalition hit back, and Egypt approved military support for Riyadh."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 25 (down from 28): Saudi, Turkish and Pakistani envoys met Iran's leaders, Iran says indirect US talks continue, and Putin hosts Iran's president Tuesday."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 24 (up from 22): no explicit nuclear threats, but Trump publicly named Iran's Pickaxe Mountain nuclear-linked site as a target."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,677 Monday (+0.7%) as Anthropic's IPO filing lifted AI and chip stocks; still about 2% below its 22 Oct peak."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +0.3% Monday, lagging tech."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +0.8% Monday as chips jumped 2.8%; Big Tech earnings Wed-Thu are the real test."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.99% (Monday, flat): high, as markets wait for Wednesday's Fed."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$101.8 settle Monday (−1.5%), and a bit lower early Tuesday, still above $100."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$115.8 (−0.8% Monday) as regional envoys met Iran's leaders; still near a six-month high."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.35/gal (AAA, 26 Oct), creeping up and just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,012: back above $4,000 as lower oil eased inflation fears before the Fed."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$80k = neutral: it is hovering around $80,000 before the Fed; ~$78k is support."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% now; a hike would make borrowing dearer. Decision Thu 1am Bangkok."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 10% for 28 Oct (over 90% hold); over 70% for a hike by year-end as oil stays high."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. The dollar edged higher early Tuesday."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~156.9 = little changed; the BOJ meets 29-30 Oct."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. 1.00%; economists (KResearch, InfoQuest consensus) expect a hold on Wed 28 Oct, and Kalshi traders put a hold at ~97%+."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. SET 1,579.03 (+1.05% Mon 26 Oct), led by PTT, DELTA, banks and tourism; analysts see resistance 1,590 and support 1,560 today."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿3.5B on 26 Oct, their second big buy day in a row, cutting October's net selling to about −฿3.5B."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
